    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for a spark today as we navigate a slate defined by a few high-upside matchups. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) stands out as our premier start; his favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt, combined with a slow delivery from the mound that boosts his steal probability, makes him the engine of our outfield. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.86) remains a set-and-forget anchor, buoyed by a prime matchup against Cristian Javier, whose 5.27 xERA offers significant room for run production. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.72) is technically slotted lower in our rotation, he is a primary beneficiary of a positive platoon split today, offering a high-floor profile for our middle infield needs.\n\nWe are forced to navigate several lineup uncertainties, as most of our active core has yet to have their official batting order confirmed. **Nasim Nunez** (49.93) is our most precarious start; while he is a critical component of our stolen base strategy, his efficiency is hampered by an elite opposing battery in Aaron Nola that historically stifles base runners. Between him and **Andy Pages** (60.69), we are monitoring any late-breaking weather or lineup changes, as our depth is currently constrained by the absence of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jorge Polanco**, all of whom are inactive today. **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL, further thinning our options for utility pivots.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the marginal slotting of **Heliot Ramos** (54.20). Despite a decent projection, he sits on the lower end of our starting threshold; his lack of a clear pitcher matchup today creates volatility compared to the data-driven certainty of **Kyle Tucker** (65.36). We are opting to lean into **Kyle Tucker** against Matthew Boyd, trusting his veteran consistency over the relative unpredictability of the rest of our utility bench. As we look ahead, we remain cautious about the impact of the stolen base environment on **Nasim Nunez**; if his lineup position drops further, we may be forced to look toward prospects like **Jacob Wilson** or **Sam Antonacci** should they become active, but for now, the objective is to capitalize on the high-xERA starters faced by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**",
